To implement the zoom in and zoom out functionality in the Vue component, we will update the `zoomIn` and `zoomOut` methods to adjust the `zoom` data property. This will be applied to the iframe using the `style` attribute with TailwindCSS classes.

Here's how the updated component will look:

```vue /home/codx-junior/codx-junior/client/src/components/HTMLViewer.vue
<script setup>
import Code from './Code.vue';
</script>
<template>
  <div class="html-viewer-container">
    <div class="flex gap-2">
      <div class="btn btn-sm" @click="zoomOut">
        <span>-</span> <!-- Indicates zoom out -->
      </div>
      <div class="btn btn-sm" @click="zoomIn">
        <span>+</span> <!-- Indicates zoom in -->
      </div>
    </div>
    <iframe
      :srcdoc="htmlContent"
      sandbox="allow-popups allow-forms"
      frameborder="0"
      class="w-full h-96"
      :style="{ zoom: zoom }"
    ></iframe>
    <Code :text="htmlContent" text-language="html" />
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    htmlContent: {
      type: String,
      required: true,
      default: '<html><body><p>No content provided</p></body></html>'
    }
  },
  data() {
    return {
      zoom: 1 // Default zoom level
    } 
  },
  methods: {
    zoomOut() {
      // Ensure zoom level doesn't go below 0.2
      if (this.zoom > 0.2) {
        this.zoom -= 0.1
      }
    },
    zoomIn() {
      // Ensure zoom level doesn't exceed 1.5
      if (this.zoom < 1.5) {
        this.zoom += 0.1
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

### Explanation

- **HTML Template**: Added indicators `+` and `-` for zoom buttons to make them functional.
- **Props**: `htmlContent` is a required prop with a default value if none is provided.
- **Data**: We have a `zoom` property initialized to `1` representing the default zoom level.
- **Methods**:
  - **zoomIn**: Increases the zoom level by `0.1` until the maximum limit of `1.5` is reached.
  - **zoomOut**: Decreases the zoom level by `0.1` until the minimum limit of `0.2` is reached.
- **Style Binding**: The `zoom` level is set directly on the iframe using a style binding.

Here's the updated Vue component content, incorporating the use of FontAwesome icons as requested:

```vue /home/codx-junior-projects/codx-junior/client/src/components/HTMLViewer.vue
<script setup>
import Code from './Code.vue'
</script>
<template>
  <div class="html-viewer-container">
    <div class="flex gap-2">
      <div class="btn btn-sm" @click="zoomOut">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass-minus"></i> <!-- Font Awesome Icon for zoom out -->
      </div>
      <div class="btn btn-sm" @click="zoomIn">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass-plus"></i> <!-- Font Awesome Icon for zoom in -->
      </div>
    </div>
    <iframe
      :srcdoc="htmlContent"
      sandbox="allow-popups allow-forms"
      frameborder="0"
      class="w-full h-96"
      :style="{ zoom: zoom }"
    ></iframe>
    <Code :text="htmlContent" text-language="html" />
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    htmlContent: {
      type: String,
      required: true,
      default: '<html><body><p>No content provided</p></body></html>'
    }
  },
  data() {
    return {
      zoom: 1 // Default zoom level
    }
  },
  methods: {
    zoomOut() {
      // Ensure zoom level doesn't go below 0.2
      if (this.zoom > 0.2) {
        this.zoom -= 0.1
      }
    },
    zoomIn() {
      // Ensure zoom level doesn't exceed 1.5
      if (this.zoom < 1.5) {
        this.zoom += 0.1
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

### Explanation
- **FontAwesome Icons**: Replaced `+` and `-` symbols with FontAwesome icons `<i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass-plus"></i>` for zoom in and `<i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass-minus"></i>` for zoom out.
- This change enhances the UI by providing a more modern and visually appealing way to represent the zoom controls.
